Web source (spec): web/src/features/notifications/components/LegacyAlertsRedirect.tsx
  A query-aware redirect from the legacy `/alerts` route. It reads react-router
  `useLocation()`, maps the legacy `?tab=` value to the new Notifications route,
  forwards every other search param, and renders `<Navigate to={to} replace />`:
    /alerts                     -> /notifications/alerts
    /alerts?tab=alerts&filter=… -> /notifications/alerts?filter=…
    /alerts?tab=history         -> /notifications/inbox
    /alerts?tab=preferences     -> /notifications/quiet-hours
  No data fetch, no loading/empty/error/stale/offline branches — its only branches
  are the tab->route map, the absent-tab default ('alerts'), and the unknown/empty-tab
  fallback ('/notifications/alerts'). All reproduced natively (see below).

Native output (apps/apple/TeslaSync/feature-views/LegacyAlertsRedirect.*):
  LegacyAlertsRedirect.Model.swift      — pure resolver: TAB_TO_ROUTE map, default,
                                          fallback, query forwarding, and a
                                          URLSearchParams-parity query model
                                          (ordered pairs, first-value get, delete-all,
                                          application/x-www-form-urlencoded with + for space).
                                          Binds AppRoute (.notifications) for real navigation.
  LegacyAlertsRedirect.Telemetry.swift  — P1/S11 diagnostics seam (`view.opened` +
                                          redaction-safe redirect event; os_log default sink).
  LegacyAlertsRedirect.swift            — SwiftUI interstitial: spinner + localized title +
                                          destination chip + subtitle; emits view.opened and
                                          dispatches the decision to the host's navigation seam
                                          once on appear (native parity of <Navigate replace>).
                                          VoiceOver label+value, never a blank surface.
  LegacyAlertsRedirect.Previews.swift   — 6 #Preview branches (alerts+query, history->inbox,
                                          preferences->quiet-hours, unknown->fallback,
                                          no-query, Dynamic Type AX2).
  LegacyAlertsRedirect.Tests.swift      — 27 XCTest cases (resolver table, URLSearchParams
                                          parity, Location, telemetry slug + events).
  LegacyAlertsRedirect.strings          — P1/S10 i18n table (title, subtitle, 3 destinations,
                                          VoiceOver label). No hardcoded English in code.

